# Local development environment template.
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and adjust as needed.
#
# - GOOSE_* are read by `go tool goose` (it auto-loads .env from the cwd).
# - DATABASE_URL / PORT are read by the API server (loaded via godotenv in main.go).
# - In production, env vars are injected by ECS task definitions; .env is ignored.
#
# The local dev credentials below match docker-compose.yml — these are NOT secrets.

GOOSE_DRIVER=postgres
GOOSE_DBSTRING=postgres://admin:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/peopleflow_vacancies?sslmode=disable
GOOSE_MIGRATION_DIR=db/migrations
DATABASE_URL=postgres://admin:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/peopleflow_vacancies?sslmode=disable
PORT=8080

# --- Identity / JWT (auth) -----------------------------------------------
# Required to enable /me/* routes. When any of these is unset the server
# still boots, but /me/* returns 401 for every request (fail-closed).
#
# IDENTITY_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM accepts both PKCS#1 (header "RSA PUBLIC KEY")
# and PKIX (header "PUBLIC KEY") PEM blocks. Provide the public half of
# the RS256 signing key; the verifier is pinned to RS256 in code.
#
# IDENTITY_JWT_ISSUER  = expected `iss` claim (e.g. Cognito user-pool issuer).
# IDENTITY_JWT_AUDIENCE = expected `aud` claim (e.g. Cognito app-client ID).
IDENTITY_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\nREPLACE_WITH_BASE64_DER_OF_RSA_PUBLIC_KEY\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----"
IDENTITY_JWT_ISSUER=https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/REPLACE_WITH_USER_POOL_ID
IDENTITY_JWT_AUDIENCE=REPLACE_WITH_APP_CLIENT_ID

# --- Audit log: client IP and browser (audit-log-v1 §4) ----------------------
# Shared secret between the Next BFF and this API. When a request carries a
# matching X-PF-Proxy-Secret header, the audit rows take the client IP and
# browser from X-PF-Client-IP / X-PF-Client-User-Agent (ip_source = bff).
# Otherwise those headers are ignored and the API records the address it
# sees (TCP peer, or X-Forwarded-For when the peer is inside TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS;
# ip_source = peer). Unset or empty: no header is ever trusted (local dev).
# Use at least 32 random bytes (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) and give the SAME
# value to the frontend as AUDIT_PROXY_SECRET. Never commit a real value.
AUDIT_PROXY_SECRET=
# Optional, comma-separated CIDRs of the reverse proxies (e.g. the production
# ALB) whose X-Forwarded-For is honoured. Also used by the assessment rate
# limiter. Unset locally. An invalid or /0 value aborts startup.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=10.0.0.0/8
